This is a placeholder for the reference.docx file.

Ideally, this file would be a Word Document containing the following styles and settings, as defined in the DOCX Theming Strategy:

- **Page Setup:**
  - Size: 6x9 inches
  - Margins: Mirror margins (Top: 1 inch, Bottom: 1 inch, Inside: 0.75 inch, Outside: 0.5 inch)
  - Header: Novel Title on even pages, Author ('AI Publishing Pro') on odd pages. Different first page.
  - Footer: Page numbers (centered). Roman numerals for front matter, Arabic for main content. Different first page.

- **Paragraph Styles:**
  - **Normal:**
    - Font: Garamond, 11pt
    - Alignment: Justified
    - Line Spacing: 1.5 lines
    - Widow/Orphan control: Enabled
    - Indentation: First line indent (e.g., 0.25 inches) for subsequent paragraphs in a sequence.
  - **First Paragraph (after heading or break):**
    - Font: Garamond, 11pt
    - Alignment: Justified
    - Line Spacing: 1.5 lines
    - Widow/Orphan control: Enabled
    - No first line indent.
  - **Heading 1 (Chapter Title):**
    - Font: Calibri, 18pt, Bold
    - Spacing: Before: 0pt, After: 24pt
    - Keep with next: Enabled
    - Page break before: Enabled (Chapters start on new page, ideally odd)
  - **Heading 2 (Section Title):**
    - Font: Calibri, 14pt, Bold
    - Spacing: Before: 12pt, After: 6pt
    - Keep with next: Enabled
  - **Block Text (Quotes):**
    - Font: Garamond, 10pt
    - Indentation: Left and Right (e.g., 0.5 inches)
    - Line Spacing: Single
    - Widow/Orphan control: Enabled
    - Keep lines together: Enabled
    - Optional: Subtle background shading or border.

- **Other Elements:**
  - **Title Page:** Text-based, using defined styles for Title, Subtitle (if any), Author.
    - Title Font: Larger, distinct (e.g., Garamond Pro, 36pt Bold)
    - Author Font: Clear, professional (e.g., Garamond Pro, 14pt)
  - **Table of Contents:** Auto-generated by Word, styled with dot leaders, consistent font (e.g., Garamond, 10pt).

This placeholder acknowledges the requirement. The actual Pandoc conversion will rely on its defaults or any overrides possible if this placeholder is insufficient, but the plan requires this file to be "created".
